CORE libcxx
sort.cpp
--cpp17 --stdlib libc++ --unwind 8 --object-bits 12
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ sorted: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
no body for callee
--
libc++ (LLVM 18) <algorithm>: std::sort on int called
std::__sort<__less<int, int> &, int *>, which libc++ declares `extern
template' (sort.h:905) and defines only in libc++.so (src/algorithm.cpp;
the header has only the declaration, sort.h:892), so it had no body.
Fixed (round 163w): provide_stdlib_bodies models it (test_sort_types.desc).
clang++ 18 -stdlib=libc++ accepts this program, and it fails only its
WRONG assertion.
